e backup copy. Identify two risks and recommend a simple backup verification plan.\n\n\u0e1c\u0e25\u0e25\u0e31\u0e1e\u0e18\u0e4c\n\u0e02\u0e49\u0e2d\u0e21\u0e39\u0e25\u0e14\u0e34\u0e1a\n\nReliability Tradeoffs:\n- Local-only: Offers high speed and accessibility, but is vulnerable to localized disasters (fire, theft, hardware failure). It creates a single point of failure.\n- Offsite backup: Provides geographic redundancy and protection against site-specific disasters, but introduces dependency on network stability and potentially higher latency or costs.\n\nTwo Risks:\n1. Hardware/Site Failure: Local-only storage can be physically destroyed, rendering the backup useless.\n2. Data Corruption/Ransomware: If local backups are constantly connected, they can be encrypted or corrupted alongside primary data, whereas offsite/offline copies can act as an immutable barrier.\n\nRecommended Verification Plan:\n1. Monthly 'Restore Test': Attempt to restore a random file (or folder) from your backup to a different location to ensure data integrity.\n2. Automated Status Check: Enable email or push notifications for your backup software to alert you immediately if a scheduled backup fails or is missed.\n\n\u0e1c\u0e25\u0e08\u0e32\u0e01 runtime: completed\n\n\u0e17\u0e14\u0e2a\u0e2d\u0e1a\u0e40\u0e2a\u0e23\u0e47\u0e08\u0e41\u0e25\u0e49\u0e27 \u0e14\u0e39 Execution Trace \u0e2b\u0e23\u0e37\u0e2d\u0e40\u0e0a\u0e37\u0e48\u0e2d\u0e21\u0e15\u0e48\u0e2d Tree \u0e01\u0e31\u0e1a\u0e41\u0e2d\u0e1b\u0e1e\u0e25\u0e34\u0e40\u0e04\u0e0a\u0e31\u0e19\u0e44\u0e14\u0e49\n\n\u0e02\u0e49\u0e2d\u0e21\u0e39\u0e25\u0e2a\u0e33\u0e2b\u0e23\u0e31\u0e1a\u0e17\u0e14\u0e2a\u0e2d\u0e1a\n\u0e02\u0e49\u0e2d\u0e04\u0e27\u0e32\u0e21\nJSON\n\n\u0e41\u0e15\u0e48\u0e25\u0e30\u0e01\u0e32\u0e23\u0e17\u0e14\u0e2a\u0e2d\u0e1a\u0e40\u0e1b\u0e47\u0e19 Run \u0e41\u0e22\u0e01\u0e01\u0e31\u0e19 \u0e41\u0e25\u0e30\u0e43\u0e0a\u0e49 runtime \u0e40\u0e14\u0e35\u0e22\u0e27\u0e01\u0e31\u0e1a API \u0e02\u0e49\u0e2d\u0e21\u0e39\u0e2